{title: I Heard the Bells on Christmas Day}
{artist: Henry W. Longfellow / John B. Calkin}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Carol}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: i-heard-the-bells-on-christmas-day.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (I_Heard_The_Bells_On_Christmas_Day-Waltham_Calkin)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]I heard the bells on [A7]Christmas day
[A7]Their [D]old familiar carols [A7]play,
[A7]And [G]wild and [D]sweet the [F#]words re[Bm]peat
[Em]Of [D]peace [G]on [D]earth, good [A]will to [D]men.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]And thought how, as the [A7]day had come,
[A7]The [D]belfries of all Christen[A7]dom
[A7]Had [G]rolled a[D]long th’un[F#]broken [Bm]song
[Em]Of [D]peace [G]on [D]earth, good [A]will to [D]men.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Till ringing, singing [A7]on its way
[A7]The [D]world revolved from night to [A7]day,
[A7]A [G]voice, a [D]chime, a [F#]chant sub[Bm]lime
[Em]Of [D]peace [G]on [D]earth, good [A]will to [D]men.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]And in despair I [A7]bowed my head
[A7]There [D]is no peace on earth, I [A7]said,
[A7]For [G]hate is [D]strong and [F#]mocks the [Bm]song
[Em]Of [D]peace [G]on [D]earth, good [A]will to [D]men.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Then pealed the bells more [A7]loud and deep:
[A7]God [D]is not dead, nor doth He [A7]sleep;
[A7]The [G]wrong shall [D]fail, the [F#]right pre[Bm]vail
[Em]With [D]peace [G]on [D]earth, good [A]will to [D]men.
{end_of_verse}
